<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GogoStatement - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gogostatement/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gogostatement/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 150</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_150/</link><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jan 2025 13:55:19 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_150/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import (&#10; &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10; &amp;#34;time&amp;#34;&#10;)&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; ch1 := make(chan int)&#10; go fmt.Println(&amp;lt;-ch1)&#10; ch1 &amp;lt;- 5&#10; time.Sleep(1 * time.Second)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A: 5&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B: Cannot compile&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C: Runtime deadlock&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;C &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/FsQsswPtOpp" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;fatal error: all goroutines are asleep - deadlock!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Official description of &lt;a href="https://go.dev/ref/spec#Go_statements" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Go statements&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;go&lt;/code&gt; statement starts a new goroutine (concurrent thread of execution) and executes a function call in that goroutine.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>